Package: multimod
Title: Define and Render Mathematical Models Across Modeling Languages
Version: 0.5.0.9000
Authors@R:
  c(person(given = "Oleg", 
          family = "Lugovoy", 
          email = "olugovoy@optimalsolution.dev", 
          role = c("aut", "cre"), 
          comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5546-9875")))
Copyright: The example_models dataset contains content derived from energyRt,
    copyright the energyRt development team; see inst/COPYRIGHTS.
Description: A unified framework for mathematical model representation,
    analysis, transformation, and optimization. Uses an intermediate
    representation to construct, import, inspect, simplify, and export
    mathematical models independently of modeling languages and solvers.
    Reads 'GAMS' and 'GNU MathProg' models; writes 'GAMS', 'GNU MathProg',
    'JuMP', 'Pyomo' and 'LaTeX'; generates and reduces linear programming
    matrices for solving with 'HiGHS' or 'cuOpt', and decodes the
    solutions. Currently focused on continuous linear optimization.
